# Shell scripts must keep LF in the working tree, not just in the index.
#
# Docker COPYs the working-tree file, so on a Windows checkout a CRLF
# entrypoint.sh ships a `#!/bin/sh\r` shebang. The kernel then looks for an
# interpreter literally named `/bin/sh\r`, and the container dies on a loop
# with "exec /entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory" - which names the
# script, not the interpreter, and so reads as a missing file rather than a
# line ending.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are read inside the build, where CR is not whitespace.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
